<title>USA: Hanger Q4 oper shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Hanger Q4 oper shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>BETHESDA, Md. 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr loss	    $0.07   profit	 $0.07</p>
<p> Net shr loss		0.08   profit	  0.07</p>
<p> Oper Net loss		657   profit	   547</p>
<p> Net loss		     741   profit	   547</p>
<p> Net Sales		 26,027		   13,357</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted   9,526,702		8,290,544</p>
<p>		     YEAR</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.12		    $0.26</p>
<p> Net shr		     0.11		     0.26</p>
<p> Oper net		   1,084		    2,135</p>
<p> Net			  1,000		    2,135</p>
<p> Net Sales		 66,806		   52,468</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted   8,791,519		8,290,544</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share and average share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: About $2.5 million of pre-tax non-recurring costs charged in Q4 1996 were in connection with Hanger's acquisition of JEH and the integration of JEH's operations with those of Hanger's.</p>
<p>An $84,00 after-tax extraordinary item in Q4 1996 related to Hanger's refinancing of existing bank debt.</p>
